Adds a system that allows easter eggs to be defined within the app. Easter eggs (referred to as "eggs"), can be defined in an `eggs.json` file with the following schema:
```jsonc
[
  // Each object in the array is an egg
  {
    // The 'match' property contains a list of matchers. If any of them resolve as true, the egg is considered to be matched.
    // All terms are compared to a lowercased seed, and thus should also be provided in lowercase.
    // See the 'matchers' object in eggs.js for a full list
    "match": {
      "all": ["terms"], // the seed must contain all the listed terms
      "any": ["terms"], // the seed must contain any of the listed terms
      "exact": ["terms"] // the seed must exactly be any of the listed terms
    },
    // The 'mutate' property contains a list of mutations. All of them get executed in order. 
    // See the 'mutations' object in eggs.js for a full list
    "mutate": {
      "background": "red", // Sets the background property of the body element
      "css": "body { background: 'red'; }" // Adds a new style tag with the given content
    }
  }
]
```

Eggs are matched against the current page's seed, forced to lowercased. Multiple eggs can match for a given seed, which could lead to interesting (or deadly) combinations. The list of matchers and mutations can be expanded at the contributor's discretion.

